Installation
https://github.com/yaskawa-global/motoros2_client_interface_dependencies
Checking MotoPlus configuration

Use the following steps to verify MotoPlus has been correctly configured for MotoROS2, and the necessary settings are active:

    boot the controller while holding {MAIN MENU} on the pendant keypad to enter Maintenance mode
    upgrade to MANAGEMENT security level by touching [System Info]→[Security] (default password is all 9's)
    touch [System Info]→[Setup] and select OPTION FUNCTION
    move to MotoPlus FUNC., make sure it is set to USED. If it isn't, set it to USED
    move cursor down to MOTOMAN DRIVER and make sure it is set to USED. If it isn't, set it to USED

Installing MotoROS2 out file

Place the .out (main binary), .yaml (configuration), and .dat (I/O names) files on an external storage device: Compact Flash (CF), Secure Digital (SD), and USB sticks can be used depending on the controller model. Insert the storage device into the robot's programming pendant.

If the controller is configured with the Functional Safety Unit (FSU), then SAVE DATA CRC CHECK FUNC (FSU) must be temporarily disabled during the installation procedure.

Turn on the robot controller to enter Normal Operation mode.

In Normal Operation mode:

    upgrade to SAFETY security level by touching [System Info]→[Security] (default password is all 5's)
    touch [Setup]→[Function Enable]
    navigate to SAVE DATA CRC CHECK FUNC (FSU)
    set this feature to INVALID
    turn off the robot controller

Turn on the robot controller while holding the {Main Menu} key on the keypad to enter Maintenance mode. You may release the key when you see the Yaskawa logo appear on the screen.

In Maintenance mode:

    upgrade to MANAGEMENT security level by touching [System Info]→[Security] (default password is all 9's)
    touch [MotoPlus APL]→[Device] to select CF, SD, or USB memory type
    touch [MotoPlus APL]→[Load (User App)] to select and load the mr2_*_*.out file
    touch [MotoPlus APL]→[File List] and verify that MotoROS2 was properly installed and no other MotoPlus applications are currently loaded on the controller
    (YRC1000[micro] only): touch [File]→[Initialize] and select USER DEFINED FILES
    (YRC1000[micro] only): select SRAM RAM DRIVE and initialize it
    rotate the pendant key-switch (upper left of pendant) fully counter-clockwise into TEACH mode
    reboot the robot controller into regular mode

In Normal Operation mode:

    you will get alarm 8013 [0] Missing MotoROS2 cfg file. touch [RESET] to clear the alarm
    upgrade to MANAGEMENT security level by touching [System Info]→[Security] (default password is all 9's)
    touch [PARAMETER]→[S2C] and set the following parameters:
        S2C541 = 0
        S2C542 = 0
        S2C1102 = 2
        S2C1104 = 2
        S2C1117 = 1 (DX200 only)
        S2C1250 = 1
        S2C1402 = 3

If a custom INFORM job will be used:

    touch [EX MEMORY]→[Load]
    cursor to JOB and press [SELECT]
    cursor to your job file and press [SELECT] then [ENTER]

YRC1000 and YRC1000 micro

    touch [EX MEMORY]→[Load]
    cursor to USER DEFINED FILES and press [SELECT]
    cursor to motoros2_config.yaml and press [SELECT] then [ENTER]

DX200

    power down the DX200 controller
    copy the motoros2_config.yaml file to a USB storage drive
    insert the USB drive into the CN106 USB port inside the controller cabinet
    leave the drive in place and close the controller cabinet
    power up the DX200 controller

Note: on DX200, the USB stick used to store motoros2_config.yaml can't be removed, it must remain inserted into the USB port labelled CN106, or at least as long as MotoROS2 is installed on the controller. Without the USB stick in CN106, MotoROS2 would not be able to load its configuration and alarms will be raised on each controller (re)boot.
All supported controllers

Within 30 seconds of loading the configuration file, you should get alarm 8001[10] Speed FB enabled, reboot now. Reboot again and there should be no alarms.

If you receive any errors or alarms after rebooting, please refer to the Troubleshooting section for information on how to remedy the issue.

If SAVE DATA CRC CHECK FUNC (FSU) was disabled at the start of this procedure, then it can now be reenabled.

    upgrade to SAFETY security level by touching [System Info]→[Security] (default password is all 5's)
    touch [Setup]→[Function Enable]
    navigate to SAVE DATA CRC CHECK FUNC (FSU)
    set this feature to VALID

